<p>Saudi Arabia said attacks on its energy infrastructure cut oil production capacity by about 600,000 barrels per day and reduced East-West pipeline throughput by around 700,000 barrels per day, according to April 9 and 10 reports citing the kingdom&#x27;s energy ministry and state news agency SPA. The reported damage hit refineries, oil fields, petrochemical plants, and other energy sites. Saudi reports said the disruptions affected Riyadh, the Eastern Province, and Yanbu Industrial City.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Cumulative toll: SPA said the reported disruption included earlier strikes on some facilities, suggesting the damage came from more than a single round of attacks.</li><li>Utility reach: Saudi reports said electricity facilities were also disrupted, showing that the impact extended into the kingdom&#x27;s power network.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Saudi energy ministry: SPA attributed the loss figures to an official source at the energy ministry, indicating that they reflect Saudi Arabia&#x27;s own assessment of the attacks&#x27; operational impact. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/attacks-cut-saudi-oil-output-and-east-west-pipeline-flow-state-news-agency-says'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Saudi state media reporting: The disclosure stood out because Saudi Arabia had not previously detailed how the attacks affected oilfield production. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/attacks-cut-saudi-oil-output-and-east-west-pipeline-flow-state-news-agency-says'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Market-focused coverage: NDTV highlighted that missile and drone barrages reached oil fields deep in the desert, along with refineries and petrochemical plants, underscoring the breadth of supply exposure. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/saudi-oil-output-capacity-pipeline-flows-cut-in-supply-risk-11337043#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/saudi-oil-output-capacity-pipeline-flows-cut-in-supply-risk-11337043#publisher=newsstand'>Saudi Oil Output Capacity, Pipeline Flows Cut in Supply Risk</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/attacks-cut-saudi-oil-output-and-east-west-pipeline-flow-state-news-agency-says'>Saudi Arabia says attacks cut oil output and East-West Pipeline flow</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/attacks-cut-saudi-oil-output-and-east-west-pipeline-flow-state-news-agency-says'>Attacks cut Saudi oil output and East-West pipeline flow, state news agency says</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lse.co.uk/news/ebrd-to-deploy-5-billion-euros-in-countries-hit-by-iran-war-xolgni9ibt6tlfr.html'>Saudi Arabia reports that the recent Iranian attack on a pumping station of the East–West Crude Oil Pipeline reduced its throughput by  700,000 barrels per day.</a> - lse.co.uk</li></ul>